# lidocaine.msf
# Lidocaine  pKa=7.900 (diethylammonium→amine, q=+1→0)
# Source: Avdeef 2001 / Perrin 1981
# Local anaesthetic. Tertiary amine; pKa=7.9 is critical for mechanism:
# at physiological pH 7.4, ~24% is uncharged (membrane-permeant form),
# ~76% is protonated (active receptor-binding form). The balance is
# exquisitely sensitive to pH — infected (acidic) tissue shifts equilibrium
# toward cation → reduced efficacy. Tests tertiary amine adjacent to amide.

